+# place.dem — Story 3.5: player node placement (the router toolbox). The 1.2
+# fixture is residential(0) at {8,15} ← router(1) at {20,15} → content_host(2)
+# at {32,15}. The player places a router_basic at {20,5} (clear of every
+# fixture node by ≥ the 7-tile separation radius: 10 from the fixture router,
+# ~15.6 from both terminals) — a LOGGED Cmd_Place_Router (apply tick 11, the
+# edit fast-path convention). Then a drag-draw connects the fixture router to
+# the PLACED router (id 3, span 10 ≤ standard max 14) — the placed junction is
+# wireable by the existing drag-draw, exactly the story's launchable increment.
+#
+# T2 captures: 1250ms (t25) pins the settled placement + the new pipe; 3000ms
+# pins the settled topology. T1 hashes + the replay gate pin placement +
+# draw byte-identically (the placement is a logged command, re-applied from
+# the blessed log on every replay — E10).
+seed 42
+run 4000ms
+at 500ms place router_basic 20 5
+at 1500ms draw 1 3 standard
+capture at 2500ms
+capture at 3000ms
+expect hash stable
